# L3 execution-trace vocabulary: what a run did, what it was told, and what came of it.
#
# L3 is neither of the layers below it. L1 is true because the organization declared
# it; L2 is true as of the last time somebody looked; L3 is true because it happened.
# That is a different epistemic status, not a weaker one, and the whole of this
# vocabulary follows from it:
#
#   - A trace is evidence and never truth. Nothing here may state a business or a
#     technical fact, and ontology/shapes/trace.ttl refuses a graph that tries. A
#     finding that GitHub's default branch has moved is a finding, not an observation.
#   - A run that cannot say what it was told cannot be learned from, because a failure
#     cannot be attributed between bad knowledge and bad reasoning. So trc:usedPack is
#     mandatory and names the exact verified context pack, by the digests of both of
#     its halves.
#   - A trace records structure and never payload. There is no property here for a
#     prompt, a completion, a tool argument, a tool result, an HTTP body, an
#     environment or an opaque blob, and there is no free-form attribute one could
#     arrive under instead. Adding a payload later is reversible; removing sensitive
#     data from an append-only history is not. See docs/l3-execution-trace.md.
#
# PROV-O is reused rather than re-invented. A run and its spans are prov:Activity; the
# pack it used and the rollups it produced are prov:Entity. No reasoner is ever run
# here, so the projector materializes both types and both spellings of each edge -
# see semantic_layer.trace.project - and a consumer that speaks only PROV can read a
# summary without ever having been told about this vocabulary.
#
# Enforcement is SHACL, not a reasoner. rdfs:domain and rdfs:range below are
# documentation for external consumers; no inference is ever run over this vocabulary.

@prefix trc:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Semantic layer execution-trace vocabulary (L3)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Recorded runtime evidence: what a run was told, what it did, and what came of it. Evidence, never truth." ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    owl:imports <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/core> .

## The activities: what happened.

trc:Run
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Run" ;
    rdfs:comment """One execution, from the moment it was given a context pack to the moment it
produced an outcome. It is named by its OpenTelemetry trace id, so the evidence here and the trace
in whatever tracing system the fleet already runs are the same run rather than two records of it.""" .

trc:Span
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Span" ;
    rdfs:comment """One timed operation inside a run, shaped like an OpenTelemetry span: an
operation name, a kind, an interval, a status, and a parent. Span detail is the half of a trace
that expires; everything a run is judged by afterwards is a rollup that does not.""" .

## The entities: what was used, and what came of it.

trc:ContextPack
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Context pack" ;
    rdfs:comment """The exact pack a run was given, named by a digest over both of its halves. It
is not a copy of the pack and not a path to one: it is the identity of bytes that were verified
against a consumer instant before the run was recorded, which is what makes 'what did this run
know' a question with one answer.""" .

trc:Outcome
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Outcome" ;
    rdfs:comment "How a run ended, as one of a closed set of states. One per run, and it outlives the span detail the run was made of." .

trc:Metric
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Metric" ;
    rdfs:comment "One named, typed measurement a run rolled up. Kept indefinitely, because a number is what a fleet is steered by long after the spans behind it have expired." .

trc:Finding
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Finding" ;
    rdfs:comment """Something a run noticed, as a code and a severity, optionally about one L1 or
L2 node. It is a report and not a correction: a finding never changes what it is about, and
promotion of a finding into a proposal is a later phase.""" .

## Run attributes.

trc:traceId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "trace id" ;
    rdfs:comment "The OpenTelemetry trace id, as 32 lower-case hex characters. Carried as an attribute as well as in the identifier so a reader never has to decode an IRI to join this run to an APM." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Run ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:usedPack
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:used ;
    rdfs:label "used pack" ;
    rdfs:comment """Read: this run was given that context pack, and nothing else. Exactly one, and
it is the most important cardinality in the model: without it there is no record of what the agent
was told, so a failure cannot be attributed between bad knowledge and bad reasoning and the
evidence is unusable.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Run ;
    rdfs:range trc:ContextPack .

trc:hasOutcome
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "has outcome" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this is how the run ended. Exactly one: a run with two outcomes has none a reader can act on, and a run with none was never finished." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Run ;
    rdfs:range trc:Outcome .

trc:spanDetailExpiredAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "span detail expired at" ;
    rdfs:comment """The retention horizon that removed this run's span detail. It is written when
retention runs rather than inferred from the absence of spans, so a summary says 'the detail
expired' instead of leaving a reader to conclude 'the run recorded nothing'.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Run ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

## Span attributes.

trc:ofRun
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "of run" ;
    rdfs:comment """Read: this record belongs to that run. One property for the spans, metrics and
findings alike, because what each of them needs to say here is the same sentence; which PROV edge
that becomes - prov:wasInformedBy for an activity, prov:wasGeneratedBy for an entity - is decided
by the projector, which knows the class.""" ;
    rdfs:range trc:Run .

trc:spanId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "span id" ;
    rdfs:comment "The OpenTelemetry span id, as 16 lower-case hex characters, unique within its run." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:parentSpan
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasInformedBy ;
    rdfs:label "parent span" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this span happened inside that one. Absent on the run's root span, and never pointing outside its own run." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span ;
    rdfs:range trc:Span .

trc:operation
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "operation" ;
    rdfs:comment """What the span was doing, as a short slug from the writer's own vocabulary:
'verify-pack', 'reconcile'. It is deliberately not free text. An operation name is the one field on
a span a payload could plausibly arrive in, so it is narrowed to a shape a prompt cannot be written
in rather than trusted to be short.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:spanKind
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "span kind" ;
    rdfs:comment "The OpenTelemetry span kind: 'internal', 'server', 'client', 'producer' or 'consumer'." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:spanStatus
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "span status" ;
    rdfs:comment """The OpenTelemetry span status: 'unset', 'ok' or 'error'. There is no
accompanying status message, because a message is where the exception text, and with it the
payload, would arrive.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:touched
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "touched" ;
    rdfs:comment """Read: this span acted on that L1 or L2 node. The reference is bounded by being
an identifier this layer mints: a value that does not parse as one is refused, so the edge cannot
become a place to write a URL, a path or a sentence.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Span .

## Context pack attributes.

trc:contentDigest
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "content digest" ;
    rdfs:comment "The SHA-256 of the pack content the run was given, as 'sha256:<hex>', taken from the bytes that were verified rather than from what the manifest claimed about them." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:ContextPack ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:manifestDigest
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "manifest digest" ;
    rdfs:comment """The SHA-256 of the pack manifest, as 'sha256:<hex>'. Both halves are recorded
because a pack is two files: the manifest is what a consumer reads without parsing the content, and
a binding that named only the content could not tell two packs apart by what they claimed.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:ContextPack ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:packObservation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "pack observation" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: the pack this run used carried that L2 observation. Naming it is not asserting it: L3 points at observed truth and never states any." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:ContextPack .

trc:packSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "pack source" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: the observation in that pack was read from that source. Recorded because an identifier means nothing outside the source that issued it." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:ContextPack .

trc:packTarget
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "pack target" ;
    rdfs:comment "What the pack's observation was about, in the source's own terms: 'vvonkledge/siana'. Copied from the verified manifest, never from the caller." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:ContextPack ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

## Outcome, metric and finding attributes.

trc:outcomeStatus
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "outcome status" ;
    rdfs:comment "How the run ended: 'succeeded', 'failed' or 'blocked'. A closed set, so counting outcomes across a fleet is arithmetic rather than string matching." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Outcome ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:metricName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "metric name" ;
    rdfs:comment "What was measured, as a slug, unique within its run." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Metric ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:metricValue
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "metric value" ;
    rdfs:comment """The measurement, as a whole number. Integers only, so the same measurement
serializes to the same bytes on every machine and two summaries of one run can be compared by
hashing them.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Metric ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

trc:metricUnit
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "metric unit" ;
    rdfs:comment "What the value counts: 'count', 'millisecond' or 'byte'. A number whose unit is implied is a number somebody will read in the wrong one." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Metric ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:findingCode
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "finding code" ;
    rdfs:comment """What was found, as a slug from the writer's own closed vocabulary:
'stale-pack', 'branch-moved'. There is no accompanying description, because a description is where
the tool output would arrive; what a code means belongs in the writer that mints it.""" ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Finding ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:findingSeverity
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "finding severity" ;
    rdfs:comment "How much the finding matters: 'info', 'warning' or 'error'. A closed set, so a fleet can be filtered by it." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Finding ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

trc:findingAbout
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace> ;
    rdfs:label "finding about" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this finding is about that L1 or L2 node. Bounded the same way trc:touched is, and asserting nothing about what it points at." ;
    rdfs:domain trc:Finding .
